#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Native evidence probe for census rows 2, 3 and 6: the three causes only a real 120 Hz window shows.

  flea-census-probe run PROBE --root ROOT --flea TREE [--samples N] [--out-parent DIR] [--no-stamps] [--dry]
  flea-census-probe summary JSONL...       the ranges, each with its n, as text
  flea-census-probe parse STAMPED.log      the Qt timing events of a stamped log, one JSON object a line
  flea-census-probe clean OUTROOT          remove an output root this probe made, by absolute path, marker checked
  flea-census-probe selftest               parsers, slots, stats, trash rule and core lists on sample lines, no display

PROBE is one of: held (row 2), ops (row 6), paste (row 6), dual (row 3). ROOT is the census fixture root
tools/flea-field-instant fixtures built, TREE the Flea tree under test. Run it on minipc in a booked block with the
display idle, as flea-field-instant is run: it reuses that tool's session, recorder, uinput keys, loads and isolation.
It writes only under one mktemp -d root of its own (marker .flea-census-probe) and prints the path; clean removes it.

Qt's own timing is the instrument. Every session runs with QT_LOGGING_RULES="qt.scenegraph.time.renderloop=true;
qt.scenegraph.time.texture=true;qt.scenegraph.time.glyph=true", QSG_RENDER_TIMING=1 and QS_NO_FILTER_QT_LOGS=1. The category
names and the QSG_RENDER_TIMING variable are in libQt6Quick (strings of 6.8.2 here), and QT_LOGGING_RULES and
QS_NO_FILTER_QT_LOGS are in the quickshell binary (0.3.0 here), which filters Qt logs unless the second is set. The lines
the threaded render loop prints, per window, are:
  [gui thread] polishAndSync: start, elapsed since last call: N ms
  [gui thread] Frame prepared, polish=N ms, lock=N ms, blockedForSync=N ms, animations=N ms
  [render thread P] syncAndRender: start, elapsed since last call: N ms
  [render thread P] syncAndRender: frame rendered in Nms, sync=N, render=N, swap=N
  [render thread P] syncAndRender: last retrieved GPU frame time was F ms
and the basic loop prints "[gui thread] syncAndRender: frame rendered in Nms, polish=, sync=, render=, swap=,
perWindowFrameDelta=". Texture work: "atlastexture upload enqueued in: Nms (WxH)" and the glyph "distancefield:" line.
Qt prints whole milliseconds, so a 120 Hz frame of 8.3 ms is read to 1 ms: every figure here is a range with its n.
The lines carry no clock. A tail thread polls the session log every POLL_S and stamps each batch with CLOCK_MONOTONIC, so
a stamp is up to POLL_S after the line's print; frame times and framecap F lines (presentation ns) share that clock.
A run that reads no timing line ends with an error row that says so (held stops after its first sweep, ops and dual finish
their samples first, so those rows carry zero qt figures): the error row, not a zero, is the verdict.

held: j held on the 10k folder in list (control), columns and grid, series_held's hold; per sweep, per repeat slot
(anchor + k * interval, half an interval either side, the slot rule of held_analysis), drawn or missed, the GUI thread's
work (polish + animations), the sync handshake (sync, blockedForSync) and the render thread's work (render + swap) that fell
in it, the frames printed, and the largest gap between GUI frames. A missed slot gets a verdict: no-frame (no loop line
at all), light (every part under SMALL_MS), or the part that was largest: gui, sync or render.
ops: op.copy.large, op.copy.long, op.move.cross-fs, op.trash through series_op unchanged, each sample also carrying: the F
lines around its first changed frame (a miss: the first 40 after the paste), statusActivityState read at STAMP_S after the
paste (an IPC call each, a small perturbation; --no-stamps drops them), render and GUI work in 100 ms bins for 3 s, and in
one facts row the device of the sandbox, the op directories, the home Trash Flea sees and the real one, whether Flea's
trash renames in place (src/backend/hometrash.rs same_filesystem) and the directory GLib picks.
paste: five fresh op.copy.many sessions of three pastes each, so n=5 cold (the first paste of a session builds
CollideHost) and n=10 warm. Each paste is followed by a burst of "ready" IPC calls for BURST_S; the GUI thread serves
them, so the largest round trip over the idle median is the longest the GUI thread was away. Paste takes no stamps: their
IPC calls would queue the burst's own. The Qt GUI frame gaps and the dest refresh of the 1000 rows ride in the same row.
dual: nav.dual.down and nav.dual.up (series_pairs) in the p7-load session under: b (the census load b, a Flea copy to the
USB stick), d (dd direct writes to it, the census load d), pin (Flea pinned to FLEA cores, no load, the control), burn-off
(pin, plus one CPU burner per BURN core, on cores Flea may not use) and burn-on (pin, plus burners on Flea's own cores).
If burn-off is as slow as b, the cost is not CPU contention; if burn-on is slow and burn-off is not, it is.
FLEA cores default to the first half of the allowed cores, BURN to the next ones but the last (left to the compositor and
this tool); --flea-cores and --burn-cores override. A pinned Flea differs from the census, which is why pin is its own arm.
